  "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-1))(x-4\\text{i})(x-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 2(x+1)({x}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 2(x+1)({x}^{2}+16) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+16x+16) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x+32.$",
